  </p>

  <h2>What Fallow does, and what it does not promise</h2>
  <p>
    Fallow uses Apple's Screen Time frameworks to shield the apps you select outside a daily
    free window that you set. It is a tool that helps you keep a decision you already made.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      It is not a medical device, a clinical treatment, or a substitute for professional help
      with compulsive behaviour or addiction.
    </li>
    <li>
      It is not a security or supervision product. It is designed for the person using the
      device, not for controlling someone else's.
    </li>
    <li>
      It depends on Apple's frameworks and on your device settings. We cannot guarantee that
      every app is blocked in every circumstance, or that the app is free of faults.
    </li>
    <li>
      You keep control of your own device throughout. Nothing in Fallow prevents you from
      removing it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not copy, resell, rent or redistribute Fallow. Do not reverse engineer, decompile or
    modify it, except to the extent the law expressly allows despite this restriction. Do not
    use it to interfere with anyone else's device.
  </p>

  <h2>Subscription, free trial and Lifetime Unlock</h2>
  <p>
    Fallow offers two paid options. The exact price is shown in the app and on the App Store
    listing, in your local currency, before you confirm anything.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Yearly subscription.</strong> An auto renewable subscription billed once a year.
      It opens with a one week free trial for eligible new subscribers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Lifetime Unlock.</strong> A one time purchase. It does not renew and is not a
      subscription.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The subscription renews automatically at the end of each year unless you cancel it at
    least 24 hours before the current period ends. Your Apple Account is charged for renewal
    within 24 hours of the end of the period. If you buy a subscription before a free trial
    finishes, the unused part of the trial is forfeited.
  </p>
  <p>
    All payments are handled by Apple. We never see or store your payment details.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    You manage and cancel the subscription in your Apple Account settings, not in Fallow.
    Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription on its own.
  </p>
  <p>
    Refunds are handled by Apple under their own policy. The developer cannot cancel a
    subscription or issue a refund on your behalf, so please raise those with Apple directly.
    Where consumer law in your country gives you additional cancellation or refund rights,
    those rights still apply and nothing here removes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Price and feature changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may change the price of the subscription or what the paid tiers include. Changes to a
    subscription price take effect from a following billing period, and Apple notifies you in
    advance so you can decide whether to continue. The Lifetime Unlock, once bought, is not
    charged again.
  </p>

  <h2>Apple's role in this</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are between you and the developer only. Apple is not responsible for Fallow
    or its content. Specifically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Apple has no obligation to provide any maintenance or support for Fallow. Support
      questions go to the developer, at the address below.
    </li>
    <li>
      If Fallow fails to conform to any warranty that applies, you may tell Apple, and Apple
      will refund the purchase price. To the maximum extent the law allows, Apple has no
      other warranty obligation of any kind for Fallow.
    </li>
    <li>
