  <p>
    Fallow is provided as it is, without warranties of any kind beyond those that cannot be
    excluded by law. We do not promise that it will be uninterrupted, error free, or fit for
    any particular purpose you have in mind.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits on liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or
    for loss arising from your use of, or inability to use, Fallow. Nothing here limits
    liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything
    else that cannot lawfully be limited. Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited
    to the amount you paid for the app in the twelve months before the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Fallow collects no data. What the app stores, and where, is set out in the
    <a href="/fallow/privacy-policy" class="text-link">Fallow Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change, the updated version is published here and the date at the top
    changes with it. Continuing to use Fallow after that means you accept the new version.
    The current version took effect on <time datetime="2026-08-04">4 August 2026</time>.
  </p>

